  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Mohammad Bilal Kashim Shaikh vs The State Of Maharashtra on 10 October, 2023 2023:Bhc-As:30023 Pmb 25.ba.876-23.doc In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Bail Application No.876 Of 2023 Vs. The State Of Maharashtra .. Respondent ------------ Adv. Hasan Sayed i/b. Adv. Mohd. Muqim Khan for the Applicant. Ms. Rutuja Ambekar, App for the State. ------------ Coram : M. S. Karnik, J. Date : October 10, 2023 P.C. :",
    "facts": "3. The date of the incident is 15.10.2021. The incident happened in the running train near Kasara Railway Station. There are in all three accused. The applicant is the accused No.2. The accused No.3 is still absconding. The three accused demanded some extortion money from the victim. When he refused to pay the money the victim was assaulted by a knife and blade. 4. Learned APP opposed the application for bail. Learned APP submitted that blood stained clothes are recovered at the instance of the applicant. 5. There is no recovery of the weapon at the instance of the present applicant. The applicant was arrested on 15.10.2021. He is 18 years of age. The applicant is in custody almost for two years. There are no criminal antecedents reported against the applicant. The investigation is complete and the charge-sheet has been filed.",
